# Vulnerabilities accepted on purpose, so the Trivy gate doesn't block on them.
#
# Rules for adding an entry (reviewed in the PR like any other code change):
#   - one CVE per line, with a comment above it saying WHY it's safe to accept
#     (e.g. "code path not reachable: we never parse untrusted XML"),
#   - who accepted it and an expiry date - revisit it then, don't let it rot,
#   - never ignore something just to get a build green; upgrade the package or base image first.
#
# Example:
#   # Not reachable: only affects the CLI tool, not the library we import. Accepted by <name>, review by 2027-01-31.
#   CVE-2024-00000
#
# (empty: nothing accepted yet)
